{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T081303Z_dev-01_staged_2a98", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "For the SFDM benchmark (m_ψ=47.75 GeV, m_h2=14.325 GeV, r=0.3), the paper gives Br(h2→b b̄)=0.7910, Br(h2→c c̄)=0.1281 and Br(h2→τ⁺τ⁻)=0.0797. The 4b final state accounts for about 62.6% of h2h2 decays. This matches 0.7910², which is about 0.626.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "7.2"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 8.395, "tool_calls": 3, "tool_result_chars": 10370, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 364, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7172, "cache_read_input_tokens": 12822, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:13:11+00:00"}
